{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232814-war-and-stratagems","id":1232814,"title":"War and stratagems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-06T00:39:24-07:00","id":1232814,"title":"War and stratagems","content":"So, we've arrived at the point in my campaign when armies start marching over the landscape (or under the sea as the case may be) and darken the sky with their dust. <br /> <br /> My plucky circle and their allies have to contend not only with a full Prasadi legion with DB officiers, but also with a horde of Sea People planning to plunder the coastal cities.<br /> <br /> So I want to hear about your own battles! What epic stratagems did your PCs put into place? How did their tactics save the day (or why did they fail miserably)? What historical inspiration did you draw from and how did you adapt it to Exalted?<br /> <br /> Tell me, o Maiden of the red star, of glorious and futile battles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T09:51:29-07:00","id":1232873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232814-war-and-stratagems#post1232814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I want to hear about your own battles! What epic stratagems did your PCs put into place?</div> </div> </div> </div>The PCs had finally arrived on the Isle of the Three Dragons, where a trio of Shogunate-era Dragon-Blooded bound 101 demons to tend to their secret pirate fortress. In the time since the Three Dragons disappeared from history, the demons overran the island, which sailors learned to avoid as a haunted place.<br /> <br /> But the circle had to make haste, for the Wyld Hunt was on their very heels.<br /> <br /> \u200bMost of the more martially-inclined demons had united under the banner of a silverback blood-ape named Marrow. He and his favored lieutenants wore perroneles to battle, and kept a handful of sesseljae on hand to heal their wounds. They also had the advantage of the fort's defenses, including portcullises that defenders could materialize and dematerialize at will, and a special flood-chamber made to expel invaders.<br /> <br /> Barbus had dots in War, but hadn't bothered with a lot of the stratagem Charms; we rolled, and nobody really won over the other, so battle proceeded normally. It was a hard fight, but the PCs slew or routed the hostile demons*, proceeded to the center chamber of the fortress-manse, and attuned to it to gain control over the remaining demons.<br /> <br /> So, on, then, to the Wyld Hunt. I gave Barbus the bonuses for obtaining concrete advantages over the enemy forces, since he'd repeatedly bloodied their noses in earlier fights (including killing Peleps Deled!); he selected the Pincer stratagem; he and his tiger-warriors on one side of the isle, and Misu and his sea-devils on the other, and both peppered with the remaining demons as backup.<br /> <br /> Over a thousand soldiers died on the Realm's side, including a half-dozen of their Dragon-Blooded, while the circle only saw about a dozen fatalities amongst their pirate-crews.<br /> <br /> Nellens Malakai was among the survivors on the side of the Wyld Hunt, and a previous captive of the PCs. Knowing them to not be entirely unreasonable, he and another scion of his house came in secret to the PCs and brokered an agreement; they would report victory, and bring back sorcerously-fabricated &quot;bodies&quot; as proof of such, while the circle would lay low, adopt new names, and cease operating openly in the Neck. The bodies would also serve as arcane links to the PCs, so any screwing around on their part could be met with sorcerous retribution, in addition to the normal consequences of violating the Eclipse oath that Misu sanctified between them.<br /> <br /> I'll have to really dig around for some of the other good bits. &gt;.&gt;<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ ____________<br /> \u200b*The demons didn't <i>stay </i>dead, since the PCs didn't use spirit-killing Charms and the demons' essences were basically permanently stapled to the island's geomancy, but once the PCs had control of the island the demons had to obey their commands. Still, it was a while before the slain demons were able to put themselves back together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-06-2018, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T20:12:29-07:00","id":1233131,"title":"","content":"My PCs haven't been super into tactics. They mostly drop 2nd Circle demons on their problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T02:18:02-07:00","id":1233157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232814-war-and-stratagems#post1232814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but also with a horde of Sea People planning to plunder the coastal cities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that typically does not go well for Bronze Age cities!<br /> <br /> A few less detailed 2nd ed battles:<br /> Realm troops besieged the Dragon-King city where our Celestial PCs were. So the Lunar snuck out and cut all the officer's throats in the night. Then when they assaulted us, we lured many of them into a killing zone, and I killed like 700 in one action with Death of Obsidian Butterflies. After that the Dragon-Kings came out and routed the survivors.<br /> <br /> Our DBs attacked Lyta's island with our armies. It was a slow slog through the forest to her mountain fortress defended by a First Age weapon. Basically we just ground our way up, she came out, and a bunch of us jumped on her and killed her. Very much a traditional siege assault.<br /> <br /> Oh, and there was the one where we chased an enemy force of the Lover to a shadowland, fell upon them... and then were attacked by zombies on Autocthonian airships who'd been hiding in the Underworld to ambush us. Embaressingly obvious in retrospect.<br /> <br /> I'll continue with more detailed 3rd ed wars shortly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:15:16-07:00","id":1233160,"title":"","content":"<u>Dupree's circle vs the Crimson Masters</u><br /> <br /> The PCs had previously fought a couple of members of the Crimson Masters, a circle of ex-Cult of the Illuminated Celestials who now led a barbarian horde.<br /> The Crimson Masters were busy fighting the Realm and Sova, so decided to make peace.<br /> <br /> They sent their Eclipse to negotiate, but the PCs killed him.<br /> <br /> They later learned the Crimson Horde abandoned its eastern campaign against the Realm and Sova and was marching back across the desert to Fakel, a salt-mining city. From there they'd be able to resupply and then march north to attack the PCs' lands.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the PCs seized control of Fakel. Dupree (Twilight crafter) began to churn out swords and armour for the paramilitary pro-Lunar cultist soldiers, while Fulgens (Dawn warlord of the Djala) began to train them as Tiger Warriors.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/[img]https://preview.ibb.co/mV4RZ8/Caravan_route.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>[/IMG]<a href=\"http://\" target=\"_blank\">http://</a><a href=\"https://ibb.co/gqZ4Mo\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://preview.ibb.co/mV4RZ8/Caravan_route.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> Dupree also rebuilt the city's walls 30 foot tall and obsidian.<br /> <br /> Babar and Light (Zenith) went to negotiate with the Crimson Horde. They found an army of about 2500 Tiger Warriors... half of what they expected. Negotiations didn't go well.<br /> <br /> So Queen Enhenduanna (Eclipse sorceress) flew out on her dragon and unleashed Death Ray. Within a few rounds, she'd killed half the army, while the others broke and ran in all directions.<br /> <br /> She flew back to Fakel to find it entirely covered in mystic darkness.<br /> <br /> Under the cover of necromancy and sorcery, the other 2500 horde members had invaded Fakel from the Underworld. They looted and murdered. PCs attempted to fight back, and often did so effectively, but they were spread across the city and not coordinated. Fulgens was able to lead a small number of troops to victories across the city, but it took time.<br /> Enhenduanna managed to kill the enemy Khan (a Night Caste) and one of their Lunars, though she was badly injured, and the Horde fled back into the Underworld with their looted supplies before Fulgens could smash them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fulgens then took about 75 cavalry and went looking for the remaining half of the first army. He tracked them north through the desert, as they'd avoided Fakel and gone north towards more fertile lands. With strategic co-ordination (and good war rolls), he managed to out-manoeuvre their general. He forced her to march straight into the teeth of his ally's large levy of peasant archers, while he attacked from behind (a pincer movement).<br /> He only had 75 cavalry and about 1000+ terrified peasant archers led by a mortal King, compared to the enemy Zenith's 1000+ Tiger Warriors, but with his War buffs, bonus from strategems, etc, his 75 cavalry managed to severely damage her forces, and he fought through and defeated her himself in single combat. Then the rest of her army was easily crushed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Worried about the Underworld army, two PCs stayed to rebuild Fakel, while the others returned to their capital.<br /> <br /> But that army had lost its Night Caste Khan, and the remaining Celestials weren't very good at War, so the PCs' allies, the local Abyssal viceroys of the Forsaken Lion, were able to ambush them and defeat them.<br /> <br /> However, enough survivors escaped for a co-ordinated attack on the PCs capital. In the middle of a banquet, everyone in the PCs' temple manse was transported into the Underworld, where they were attacked by a ton of ghostly Tiger Warriors, and the ghosts of all the Solars+Lunar they'd killed. The PCs fought their way out, but the three surviving Crimson Masters escaped once more, though they'd now lost their entire army. They fled to Harborhead and took refuge with its god-blooded queen.<br /> <br /> So Ledaal Kes and his Sidereal buddies lured Light, the Zenith, to Harborhead where he was captured. The others went to save him, there was a big fight, Light lost an arm, Babar's eyes were cut out by Ahlat, and Harborhead's queen and all the remaining Crimson Masters were killed by the PCs.<br /> <br /> They'd won the war! But now Harborhead hates them, and has allied with its old colonial master, the Realm, to fight the PCs, just as Ledaal Kes planned...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:29:28-07:00","id":1233162,"title":"","content":"<u>The aftermath</u><br /> It's a year later in-character, and the game continues (but I'm not running it anymore).<br /> <br /> The Realm prepares to attack Enhenduanna's magical kingdom+allies (purple). They've got 2 legions, ships, conquered/allied countries (the PCs killed several of the leaders of the largest local country, Varamaya, so its joined with the Realm), and they're bringing troops across the pass from Prasad.<br /> Harborhead has called a ceasefire with the Realm, and is building ships to attack the Cult of the Illuminated base at Hen Ling.<br /> I tried convincing the others we should make a lightning attack against the 17th Legion and destroy the passes to Prasad, but it was felt to be unfeasible, and we're too disunited and distrustful of each other.<br /> Fulgens, Warmaster of the Djala, believes our best bet to defeat the Realm is for him to unite everyone under his rule. Obviously no-one else agrees. So he's declared war on Enhenduanna's mountain kingdom. Both I and Enhenduanna tried and failed to kill him.<br /> <br /> So the local Cult members have decided to abandon Fulgens and Enhenduanna to fight their war, and we're going to concentrate on defeating Harborhead. If we can find its shipyards, hopefully I can take my Warstrider there and smash their ships to kindling. <br /> Of course, after that, we're probably going to find that there are 2 Realm legions and a Prasadi legion right on our eastern border, completely untouched. Oh well. Maybe it'll all work itself out?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://\" target=\"_blank\">http://</a><a href=\"https://ibb.co/fDc5Bo\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://preview.ibb.co/dXJZ48/The_Great_Lake_War.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a><br /> <br /> So, the funny thing about all this, is that our PCs actually do amazingly well at pitched battles. Our Dawn defeated 2500 Tiger Warriors and a War 5 Zenith with 75 cavalry and a bunch of terrified peasant levies. Our Eclipse sorceress can blast enemy armies to pieces. But we're very bad at diplomacy, dealing with enemy sorcerers, and dealing with unorthodox tactics. And so we're in a pretty bad position.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}